Subject: Report a refused function at compile time

What this does
  Report a refused function at compile time.

Why we need it
  A function the backend refuses is only visible as "function was not lowered" when it is first called, far from the cause, and there was no way to measure how often it happens.

What it adds
  Behind `QJS_REGVM_KNOBS` and `REGVM_REPORT_DEFERRED=1`, every `goto deferred` and `unencodable = 1` site carries a reason string and prints `regvm: refused <name> (<file>:<line>): <why>` at compile time; the reasons are the inventory's rows.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
